<title>USA: USDA buys 3.60 mln lbs canned beef for programs.</title>
<headline>USDA buys 3.60 mln lbs canned beef for programs.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agricultural Marketing Service of the U.S. Department of Agriculture said it purchased 3,601,800 pounds of canned meat products on Friday at a cost of approximately $3,898,000 for use in Federal food assistance programs.</p>
<p>Details of today's purchase follow:</p>
<p>Canned Meat    Pounds	   Awarded Prices</p>
<p>Product			     dollars/lb</p>
<p>Canned Beef    3,601,800	$1.0669-$1.1139</p>
<p>Total purchases of canned meat products since the program was reopened on September 26, 1996 follow:</p>
<p>Commodity			   Cumulative</p>
<p>			    Pounds		  Dollars</p>
<p>Canned Beef	   7,347,672	     8,179,000</p>
<p>Meatball Stew	 1,296,000	     1,163,000</p>
<p>Canned Pork	   1,908,954	     2,494,000</p>
<p>Luncheon Meat	   576,000		 905,000</p>
<p>Awards made for Announcement LS-46, Invitation 10, to be shipped between Dec 28, 1996 and Jan 11, 1997.</p>
<p>Winning bidders were Dean Foods Vegetable Co (Green Bay WI) 252,126 lbs, Lakeside Foods Inc (Plainview MN) 3,349,674 lbs.</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720)</p>
</text>
